      "writtenOn": "2026-06-16T08:30:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hardcoding VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_GENERAL as the incoming layout makes sense for standard AHB producer/consumer preservation. However, hardcoding the target layout to VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_SHADER_READ_ONLY_OPTIMAL assumes the user will strictly sample this texture.\n\nAre there any consequences or expectations from Dawn\u0027s Vulkan backend regarding these hardcoded layouts? If a user imports an AHB with the intention to write to it (e.g. as a RenderAttachment), I assume Dawn will just issue a secondary layout transition internally, but I\u0027d love to check with someone with deeper Vulkan expertise (or the core Dawn team) to make sure this doesn\u0027t put Dawn into a suboptimal state.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 435,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 438,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "9c46cad9dbd826f739d0e9047d5133234c2adf46",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "14f01c66_a2f3fa86",
        "filename": "tools/android/webgpu/src/main/cpp/GPUImportedAHB.cpp",
